Chapter Title
Processing Data
Course Description
Chapter 2 introduces students to processing data using C#. Students learn how to work with variables, constants, data types, expressions, operators, input, output, and data conversion. The chapter also introduces students to performing calculations and processing information in C# applications.
Course Objectives
By the end of this chapter, students should be able to:
Understand variables and constants.
Identify and use different C# data types.
Declare and initialize variables.
Use assignment statements.
Perform arithmetic operations.
Understand expressions and operators.
Receive input from users.
Convert data from one type to another.
Process data using C#.
Display results to users.
