Learning Outcomes
After completing Chapter 2, students should be able to:
Understand the concept of variables.
Use different C# data types.
Declare and initialize variables.
Create and use constants.
Use assignment statements correctly.
Perform arithmetic operations.
Create expressions using operators.
Receive input from users.
Convert data between different data types.
Process data and display results.
