Chapter Practical Work
Students will develop simple C# programs that demonstrate:
Creating and using variables.
Working with different data types.
Performing arithmetic calculations.
Receiving user input.
Converting user input into numbers.
Processing data.
Displaying calculated results.
Example
int number1 = int.Parse(textBox1.Text);
int number2 = int.Parse(textBox2.Text);

int result = number1 + number2;

label1.Text = result.ToString();
This program receives two numbers, adds them together, and displays the result.
